---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`} description="What this site stores. Almost nothing." path="/privacy">
  <main class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Almost nothing is kept</h1>
      <p>
        Questions are processed to produce an answer and then dropped. There is no account. There is no transcript archive. A session cookie remembers only how many live questions you have used today.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rate limits use the connecting IP. Daily spend is a counter, not a dossier. Telemetry, when Cloudflare Analytics Engine is bound, records cost and degradation path. It does not record the text of the question.
      </p>
      <p>
        Voice audio is synthesized on demand and not stored. If you do not want a model in the loop, stay on the static pages. They are the product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
